hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16136","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sharik ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Zadhad Abu Umar, from Ulaym, he said: We were sitting on a roof, with us a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yazid said: I know him only as Abas al-Ghifari, and the people delve into the plague. So Abas said: O plague, take me, three times he says it. Ulaym said to him: Why do you say this? Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Let none of you wish for death, for it is at the cutting of his deeds; he is not returned so he may seek amends? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Hasten with death six: the rule of fools, and abundance of police, and sale of judgment, and blood taken lightly, and severing of kinship, and a generation who take the Quran as flutes, putting forward one to sing to them though he be least of them in understanding."
